      "dcDescription": [
        "A complete adult-size bag tunic with warp (vertical) fringes. Although this garment is made from undyed linen cloth it features several colorful elements. These include a stripe pattern of blue and undyed threads along the selvedges (the outer edges of the original fabric) as well as stripes of blue and undyed thread at the end bands which run horizontally across the bottom of the tunic. This garment was woven in one piece, then folded in half and sewn along the sides to create the tunic shape. There is evidence of mending suggesting that this piece of clothing was worn many times. For an example of an Egyptian tunic from the Late Antique/Coptic Period see museum number F 1984/11.1."
      ],
      "dcDescriptionLangAware": {
        "def": [
